+# Micro Input navigation
+
+Defines the bounded capability contract shared by the desktop bridge and renderer. Authorization precedes metadata or command access. Complete source/workspace addresses are compared exactly; empty or unknown fields are rejected. It exposes only scoped metadata index (`address`, `title`, `liveStatus`, `executionId`), exact selection (`open`), and idempotent v4 execution commands (`createSession`, `sendText`, `stop` with `expectedForegroundExecutionId`, and `query` command reconciliation) with zero transcript or search read.
